<<<
hardly. 1. Hardly)(hard. 2. Hardly... than. 3. Without h., no — hardly.
===
**hardly. 1.** *Hardly*)(*hard*. **2.** *Hardly . . . than*. **3.** *Without h., no —* *hardly*.
>>>

<<<
1. Hardly)(hard. Except in the sense scarcely, the idiomatic adverb of hard is hard, not hardly: * We worked hard, lodged hard, & fared hard ’—DeFoe.
===
**1.** *Hardly*)(*hard*. Except in the sense *scarcely*, the idiomatic adverb of *hard* is *hard*, not *hardly*: ‘ We worked hard, lodged hard, & fared hard ’—DeFoe.
>>>

<<<
It is true that in special cases hardly may or must be substituted, as in What is made is slowly, hardly, & honestly earned— Macaulay;
===
It is true that in special cases *hardly* may or must be substituted, as in *What is made is slowly, hardly, & honestly earned*—Macaulay;
>>>

